course: dictionary
lesson: 5938
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Mask is one of them. It can be a thing you wear on your face, or an action that means to hide or cover something. The words around it show you which meaning is right.
explain: «The actors wore masks on the stage.» Here a mask is a thing you wear. «The strong soap masked the smell.» Here masked is an action: the soap hid the smell. Ask yourself: is the word a thing, or is it something you do?
explain: To check your choice, put your meaning into the sentence in place of the word. If «hid the smell» makes sense, you have the right meaning for masked. If it does not make sense, try another meaning.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is called a multiple-meaning word.
fact: «Mask» can be a noun (a thing you wear) or a verb (an action): to mask something means to hide or cover it.
fact: An oxygen mask or a snorkel mask helps you breathe, for example in the air on a plane or under water when you dive.
fact: Masking tape is a paper tape used to cover the edges of things when you paint.
fact: In stories, a masked person is often a hero or a villain, hiding who they really are.
exercise: «The Greeks performed plays where the actors wore masks.» What is a mask in this sentence? | A tube for breathing under water | A paper tape for painting | *A covering worn over the face | To hide something
exercise: «The strong soap masked the smell of the drains.» What does masked mean here? | To wear on the face | *To hide or cover | To breathe deeply | To paint over
exercise: In «Put on your own oxygen mask before helping others», what kind of word is mask? | A colour | A verb: an action you do | A name for a place | *A noun: a thing you can hold
test: «The hero stood in the dark, masked and silent.» What does masked mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Hidden under the ground | *Wearing a covering over the face | Very tired and sleepy
test: Mum says, «Use masking tape around the window before you paint.» What is masking tape for? | To make a mask for Halloween | To stick paper flowers on the wall | *To cover the edges you do not want painted | To tie up the paint pot
exam: «Doctors wear masks to stop germs.» In this sentence, what does mask mean? | To hide a secret from the patients | A tube for breathing under water | *A covering over the nose and mouth | A tape used for painting
